# Employers. Written to tell the player who they actually work for: what the organisation is,
# what it does, and how it is regarded. No marketing copy — Ember is a government ship and the
# corporate presence aboard is a staffing patch — but no cleverness at the expense of substance
# either. The player is choosing an employer, not reading an epigram.

employer_name_eco = Expeditionary Corps Organisation
employer_description_eco = A state-owned limited company, and since its founding the single channel through which corporations may take part in government exploration. Officially a joint platform for industry and the state; in practice the body that decides which contractors go aboard and on what terms. Its own staff handle the paperwork, the contracts and the liaison between the Corps and everyone billing it, which makes them the least popular people in any compartment they enter.

employer_name_grayson = Grayson Manufactories Ltd.
employer_description_grayson = An industrial mining concern and one of the largest suppliers of raw materials in known space, latterly branching into assembly stock — beams, gratings, cable. Founded on Earth, moved wholesale to Mars during the collapse, and made its fortune on asteroid belt claims that turned out to sit on massive ore deposits. A member of the Big Seven, and audibly proud of it. Its people aboard are the ones who know what a bulkhead is rated for.

employer_name_aether = Aether Atmospherics and Recycling
employer_description_aether = Grew out of a transport company that spent the Earth collapse ferrying breathable air to the Lunar colonies, and stayed in the business once its engineers built a better filtration cycle than anyone else had. Now life support, gas distribution and reclamation of very nearly everything a colony throws away. Unglamorous work that everyone notices the moment it stops.

employer_name_xynergy = Xynergy
employer_description_xynergy = Founded in 2233 by a fishing skipper who took a contract to bring back a live space pike and nearly lost her ship doing it. From that beginning it became the field authority on capturing, keeping and studying xenofauna, with xenoarchaeology added as the frontier opened. Alone among the contractors aboard, its speciality is the ship's own mission.

employer_name_zenghu = Zeng-Hu Pharmaceuticals
employer_description_zenghu = One of the oldest transstellars still trading, founded as a medical research house in China and incorporated in Shanghai in 2075. Built its fortune on a patented analgesic blend and has spent the four centuries since absorbing its competitors, by negotiation where that works and by other means where it does not. Its medicine is genuinely excellent. Its business practices are a matter of record.

employer_name_nanotrasen = NanoTrasen
employer_description_nanotrasen = A research and logistics conglomerate with holdings across human space, and for a long time the name that came first in any list like this one. It no longer does. The company still runs first-rate laboratories and still supplies half the frontier, but it operates under conditions now, and its people are used to being asked about it.

employer_name_unemployed = Not employed
employer_description_unemployed = Aboard on something other than a contract. Passengers, dependants of crew, observers, and anyone between postings. Carries no obligations and no salary.
